A minimal single-machine generator, showing the sequence rollover within one millisecond:

```python
class SnowflakeGenerator:
    def __init__(self, machine_id, epoch_ms):
        self.machine_id = machine_id      # 10 bits, assigned at startup
        self.epoch_ms = epoch_ms
        self.last_ts = -1
        self.seq = 0

    def next_id(self):
        ts = current_time_ms()
        if ts < self.last_ts:
            raise ClockRolledBackError(self.last_ts - ts)
        if ts == self.last_ts:
            self.seq = (self.seq + 1) & 0xFFF   # 12-bit sequence
            if self.seq == 0:
                ts = wait_next_millis(self.last_ts)  # sequence exhausted
        else:
            self.seq = 0
        self.last_ts = ts
        return ((ts - self.epoch_ms) << 22) | (self.machine_id << 12) | self.seq
```

The rollover check (`seq == 0` after wrapping) is the part interviewers probe: if a machine issues more than 4,096 IDs in one millisecond, it must block until the next millisecond rather than silently reusing a sequence value.
